meta {
  name: Generate Grading Criteria
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/assignments/:assignment_id/grading-criteria/generate
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  assignment_id: {{assignment_id}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "assignment_text": "Write a Java program that computes the greatest common divisor GCD and the least common multiple LCM of two given integers a and b. For each input pair, print the GCD and LCM separated by a space. Each line of input contains two integers a and b separated by a space. Input consists of multiple lines and ends at EOF. Constraints: 0 < a, b <= 2000000000, LCM(a, b) <= 2000000000, and number of data sets <= 50. For each data set, print the GCD and LCM separated by a space on a single line. Example: Sample Input: 8 6, 50000000 30000000. Sample Output: 2 24, 10000000 150000000. Use Java standard input methods such as Scanner or BufferedReader to read until EOF, compute GCD using the Euclidean algorithm, compute LCM using the formula LCM(a, b) = (a * b) / GCD(a, b), ensure the output format matches exactly, and write clean readable Java code with proper syntax."
  }
}

docs {
  API 1 — Lecturer provides raw assignment text.
  AI extracts: competencies, difficulty levels, Bloom's taxonomy labels,
  marking criteria, programming language, and learning objectives.
  All results are saved as GradingCriteria rows in the database.
  Re-running this endpoint replaces any previously generated criteria for the assignment.
}
